<title>USA: Ampal-American unit sets asset sale.</title>
<headline>Ampal-American unit sets asset sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ampal-American Israel Corp said on Wednesday a subsidiary planned to sell part of a building it owned to the Israeli Government for $31 million.</p>
<p>Ampal said in a statement the subsidiary signed a letter of intent to sell the Israeli government part of a New York office building which the government already occupied.</p>
<p>The subsidiary bought the building in June 1995 for about $45 million, it said.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment on Ampal's net gain from the sale. The agreement could be signed on or before November 1, Ampal said.</p>
</text>
